## 3. Financial and Operational Alignment

The strategic targets are built upon the FY 2024 financial performance and operational metrics, as detailed in the Master Data Consistency Framework [1].

### 3.1. Financial Projections (AED)

The projected ARR growth from **AED 485,100,000** to **AED 900,000,000** by FY 2027 is the primary driver for achieving profitability. This growth assumes continued success in high-value hospital contracts (ACV target of **AED 950,000**).

| Metric | FY 2024 (Actual) | FY 2025 (Target) | FY 2026 (Target) | FY 2027 (Target) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Total ARR | 485,100,000 | 600,000,000 | 750,000,000 | 900,000,000 |
| Operating Margin | -4.1% | 2.0% | 6.0% | 10.0% |
| Net Income | -22,491,000 | 12,000,000 | 45,000,000 | 90,000,000 |

*See FIN-001 for detailed quarterly revenue and expense forecasts.*

### 3.2. Customer and Product Alignment

The focus on hospital acquisition (KR 2.1) is directly supported by the current product portfolio, which serves **520 hospitals** as of Q4 2024. The target of **900 hospitals** by FY 2027 will be achieved through cross-selling and upselling our highest-rated product, **MedSync Patient Portal** (NPS: **75**), and our core integration platform, **MedSync Connect** (NPS: **72**).

### 3.3. Headcount and People Strategy

To support the projected ARR growth, the total headcount will increase from **1,200** to **1,800** by FY 2027. This expansion will be managed alongside a reduction in voluntary attrition (KR 3.2) to ensure the retention of key talent, particularly in Engineering (**380 employees** in FY 2024) and Sales (**220 employees** in FY 2024).

